  + [138] So every intersection of $\Gamma'$ with $\beta$ lies on $\gamma_2$, after the last intersection of $\Gamma'$ with $\alpha$, and $\Gamma'$ is disjoint from $\beta$ modulo 4-disks, as $\Gamma$ is.
  + [138] If Lemma 6.4 holds, the disk sequences of $f(\Phi)\cdot\Gamma'$ and $f(\Phi)\cdot\Gamma$ are both obtained from that of $\Phi$ by replacing each 4-disk with a sign-changing 5-disk, so $f(\Phi)\cdot\Gamma'$ satisfies the parity condition because $f(\Phi)\cdot\Gamma$ does.
